  "answer": "Found the bug: `total` uses `sum -= entry.amount`. Let me check the test before fixing.\nTest uses `bun:test` and expects amounts to add (4+6=10, empty=0, single -3 → -3). Applying the one-line fix:\nFixed and verified. ✅\n\n**Summary**\n\n- **Bug:** In `src/ledger.ts`, the `total()` accumulator subtracted each entry instead of adding it (`sum -= entry.amount`), so any non-empty ledger returned the negated sum (e.g., 4 + 6 → −10).\n- **Fix:** Changed the single line to `sum += entry.amount`, so every entry adds to the running total. Negative amounts still correctly reduce the sum (they add a negative), satisfying all three expectations in the test.\n- **Preserved:** The exported shape (`interface Entry`, `export function total`) is unchanged, and `test/oracle.test.ts`, `package.json`, and `AGENTS.md` were left untouched.\n- **Test result:** `bun test` → 1 pass, 0 fail (3 `expect()` calls): `total([4,6]) === 10`, `total([]) === 0`, `total([-3]) === -3`."
